menu "dsync audio"

    config DSYNC_AUDIO_RING_KB
        int "PCM ring buffer size (KiB)"
        default 32
        range 4 128
        help
            Ring between the A2DP data callback (producer) and the I2S writer
            task (consumer). Bigger absorbs longer network stalls.

    config DSYNC_AUDIO_PREFETCH_KB
        int "Playback cushion before the writer starts (KiB)"
        default 8
        range 2 64
        help
            The writer holds off until this much PCM is buffered, which hides
            Bluetooth jitter. Larger = fewer underruns but slower start-up.
            Must stay below DSYNC_AUDIO_RING_KB.

endmenu
